  "abstract_summary": "High-resolution vision backbones have long been forced to trade away local token density to afford larger receptive fields. Hierarchical Swin transformers impose this compromise because standard windowed attention materializes an $M^2\\times M^2$ score matrix per window, incurring $O(M^4)$ memory as windows or token...",
